1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
03:17 — Autonomous Maintenance

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:14,000
An evidence-gated AI agent for safe, after-hours infrastructure change.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:24,000
The approved request is converted into an ordered execution plan.

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Every mutating step requires fresh, deterministic pre-flight evidence.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:46,000
WEB01 updates successfully. WEB02 then fails functional verification.

6
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:58,000
The agent stops, gathers evidence, and enters structured replanning.

7
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Gemini and Google ADK are invoked — but safety validation remains authoritative.

8
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:26,000
An invalid proposal is rejected. The safe fallback rolls WEB02 back and verifies v1.0.0.

9
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:38,000
The database gate detects that full web redundancy has not been restored.

10
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Database maintenance is deferred instead of risking availability.

11
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:02,000
The revised topology remains healthy while the full audit trail is preserved.

12
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:12,000
No human intervention. Twelve measured availability checks.

13
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:24,000
WEB01: updated and verified. WEB02: rolled back and verified.

14
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:36,000
Database: deferred by evidence policy. Service availability: preserved throughout.

15
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:42,000
03:17 — autonomy constrained by evidence.
